-4c2b-5d03-b5d7-fdb5074438f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193719 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193719 #edb/ref 1061 466026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193719 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c89b0360-91da-5424-aedb-da76a815447b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193719 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193720 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193720 #edb/ref 1061 466027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193720 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0da282af-995a-5faf-b0d0-876baec229e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193720 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193721 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193721 #edb/ref 1061 466031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193721 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cde1c192-24a5-5dc6-a1eb-22b02b4431e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193721 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193722 #edb/ref 1061 466034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193722 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "44d32822-3dee-5d1f-bc85-937a6b36e438" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193722 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193826 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we'll learn how to compute inverses of reciprocal functions.\n\nAs an example, let's consider the function $f(x)$, given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{7}{2x+4}\n$$\n\nTo find the inverse $f^{-1}(x)$, we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{7}{2x+4}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{7}{2y+4}\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= \\frac{7}{2y + 4} \\\\\nx(2y + 4) &= 7 \\\\\n2xy + 4x &= 7 \\\\\n2xy &= 7 - 4x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{7 - 4x}{2x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{7 - 4x}{2x}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193826 #edb/ref 1065 